+# Codex M2 local review candidate
+
+Based on WorkBuddy Lab `4b2561634b9a5c8f4978e6f7ea6978790be6fd40`.
+Not pushed, merged, deployed or independently approved.
+
+Twelve independently failing adversarial cases reproduced weaknesses in M1:
+nested numeric JSON keys could collide with string keys; strict directory scans
+used inconsistent path coordinates and admitted unrelated empty directories;
+numeric zero passed Boolean safety fields; model-card schema/identity and
+evaluation status were insufficiently checked; appending did not verify existing
+variant-log history. These are now rejected or correctly handled. Normal string
+key configurations retain their hashes and existing schema version.
+
+Hashing is integrity evidence, not authentication or research eligibility.
+Manifest files are not made immutable by filesystem permissions. Variant logs
+are single-writer; an independently trusted head/count is still needed to detect
+whole-log replacement or suffix truncation. Model-card validation is a restricted
+research-only check, not approval of performance, economics or deployment.
+
+`timebase_observation.assess_tick_clock` prepares a pure offline witness contract:
+aware UTC brackets, short monotonic-consistent collection intervals and raw tick
+epochs. It reports an offset interval without modifying epochs. Even a matching
+sample remains `TIMEBASE_UNVERIFIED` and ineligible. No live collector was run;
+independent clock synchronization, fresh quotes and historical DST evidence are
+still required. Six synthetic regressions cover +2/+3 hour contradictions, a
+matching sample across a DST-date boundary, stale ticks, clock steps and naive
+timestamps.
+
+Real-data training remains unconditionally disabled in `training_pipeline.py`,
+including when all nine supplied evidence flags claim success. No real estimator
+was trained. Synthetic fits in existing software tests are not market evidence.
+
+Python 3.12.10, pytest 9.2.0: **517 passed, 0 skipped, 0 failed**. A clean clone
+initially has **496 passed, 1 failed** because an M1 integration test reads ignored
+local `data/quarantine/USTECH100M_M5_raw.provenance.json`. The final run supplies
+only the unchanged owner-local metadata at that ignored path; no raw CSV was
+copied, no certification flag changed, and the file is not committed. Preserve
+this distinction when reproducing validation in CI. Making that existing test
+hermetic without losing the separate local-data check is a follow-up review item.
